course: dictionary
lesson: 942
title: A blockage in the pipe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A blockage is something that stops things getting through. It comes from the word block, which means to stop or close off. Look at the clues: «Fat from cooled soup rises and sets on top; poured down the sink it hardens in pipes and helps build huge blockages.» Hard fat stuck in a pipe stops the water getting through, so a blockage is something that blocks.
explain: Blockage is a noun, so you can have a blockage or several blockages. You will hear it in phrases like clear a blockage, a blockage in the drain and cause a blockage. Test your meaning in the sentence: "huge things that stop the pipe" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: The word also has a body meaning. «Only swallowing big lumps very often could cause a blockage» is about the gut, not a pipe. Ask yourself: is the blocked thing a pipe, a road, or something inside a body? The context tells you which meaning the writer wants.
fact: A blockage is something that blocks a pipe, tube, road or passage so things cannot get through.
fact: In the body, a blockage stops blood, air or food from moving, for example in a blood vessel or the gut.
fact: Choking is a blockage of the airway, and it is an emergency.
fact: Hair, fat and wet wipes are common causes of blockages in sinks, drains and toilets.
fact: «Blockage» is a noun: one blockage, many blockages.
exercise: «Fat poured down the sink can build huge blockages.» What is a blockage? | *Something that blocks a pipe so things cannot get through | A type of soap | A shiny clean pipe | A tap that drips water
exercise: «Swallowing big lumps very often could cause a blockage.» What kind of blockage is this sentence about? | A blockage in a sink | A blockage in a bag of soup | *A blockage in the gut, inside the body | A blockage on a road
exercise: Dad says, «We need to clear the blockage before the bath fills up.» What does clear the blockage mean? | Make the blockage bigger | *Remove the thing that is stopping the water getting through | Count how many blockages there are | Paint the bath
test: Which of these is a blockage in the body? | *Something stopping blood from moving inside a blood vessel | A road closed for roadworks | A pipe under the kitchen sink | A tap that has run dry
test: What is the plural of blockage? | blockage's | *blockages | blockagies | blockageses
exam: Which sentence uses blockage correctly? | She blockaged the sunny window with a smile | The bird flew high over the blockage in the sky | The soup was hot and tasty | *Hair and fat can cause a blockage in the drain
